{
 "id": 63,
 "number": 212,
 "title": "Word Search II",
 "slug": "word-search-ii",
 "category": "tries",
 "difficulty": "Hard",
 "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/word-search-ii/",
 "pattern": "Trie + backtracking on a grid",
 "statement": "Given a grid of letters and a list of `words`, return every word that can be traced on the grid by moving between horizontally or vertically neighbouring cells, using each cell **at most once** per word.",
 "example": {
  "input": "board = [[\"o\",\"a\",\"n\"],[\"e\",\"t\",\"a\"]], words = [\"oat\",\"eat\",\"tan\"]",
  "output": "[\"oat\",\"tan\"]",
  "why": "o→a→t and t→a→n can be traced through neighbouring cells. For eat, no a is next to the e."
 },
 "more": [
  {
   "input": "board = [[\"o\",\"a\",\"a\",\"n\"],\n         [\"e\",\"t\",\"a\",\"e\"],\n         [\"i\",\"h\",\"k\",\"r\"],\n         [\"i\",\"f\",\"l\",\"v\"]]\nwords = [\"oath\",\"pea\",\"eat\",\"rain\"]",
   "output": "[\"eat\",\"oath\"]"
  },
  {
   "input": "board = [[\"a\",\"b\"],[\"c\",\"d\"]], words = [\"abcb\"]",
   "output": "[]"
  },
  {
   "input": "board = [[\"a\"]], words = [\"a\"]",
   "output": "[\"a\"]"
  }
 ],
 "idea": [
  "Searching the grid separately for each word repeats a lot of work when words share beginnings.",
  "Put all the words in a **trie** and walk the grid and the trie *together*: from a cell, only continue while the trie has a branch for the next letter.",
  "Start such a walk from every cell (DFS with backtracking, marking cells as in use). Whenever the trie node marks the end of a word, that word has been found."
 ],
 "code": "class TrieNode:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.children = {}\n        self.word = None  # set on the node where a whole word ends\n\nclass Solution:\n    def findWords(self, board: List[List[str]], words: List[str]) -> List[str]:\n        root = TrieNode()\n        for word in words:\n            node = root\n            for ch in word:\n                if ch not in node.children:\n                    node.children[ch] = TrieNode()\n                node = node.children[ch]\n            node.word = word\n\n        rows, cols = len(board), len(board[0])\n        found = []\n\n        def dfs(r, c, node):\n            ch = board[r][c]\n            if ch not in node.children:\n                return\n            node = node.children[ch]\n            if node.word:\n                found.append(node.word)\n                node.word = None  # never report the same word twice\n            board[r][c] = \"#\"  # this cell is in use on the current path\n            for nr, nc in ((r + 1, c), (r - 1, c), (r, c + 1), (r, c - 1)):\n                if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols and board[nr][nc] != \"#\":\n                    dfs(nr, nc, node)\n            board[r][c] = ch  # free the cell again on the way back\n\n        for r in range(rows):\n            for c in range(cols):\n                dfs(r, c, root)\n        return found",
 "complexity": {
  "time": "O(m · n · 4ᴸ)",
  "timeWhy": "A walk starts at each of the m · n cells and branches up to 4 ways for up to L letters; the trie cuts most branches early.",
  "space": "O(total letters)",
  "spaceWhy": "The trie, plus a recursion depth of at most L."
 },
